      "created_at": "2026-09-07T21:43:43Z",
      "updated_at": "2026-09-07T21:43:43Z",
      "body": "The following is my drafted plan.\n\n1. Provide a code example illustrating how `piscina` differs from `node:worker_threads` in handling custom properties when a Native error is thrown from a worker thread, and how this could cause logical errors in an app.\n2. Provide a code example showing how to preserve these custom properties (without using third-party packages).\n3. Note that `serialize-error` can do exactly this.\n4. Add an option to automatically wrap workers with `serialize-error`.\n\n",
      "author_association": "NONE",
      "pin": null,
      "reactions": {
